  "published": "2026-11-13T19:14:39.903Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1 — Wire format fix and gRPC transport improvements\n\n• Fixed OTLP binary Protobuf field numbers to match current opentelemetry-proto spec:\n  severity_number = field 2, severity_text = field 3 (field 4 is reserved in the proto)\n  Previously used wrong field numbers which caused \"wrong wireType\" errors on all backends\n• Fixed gRPC transport for plain http:// endpoints (port 4317):\n  Added EnableMultipleHttp2Connections=true and HttpVersionPolicy.RequestVersionOrHigher\n  so .NET uses HTTP/2 instead of downgrading to HTTP/1.1 on non-TLS gRPC connections\n• Removed Google.Protobuf package dependency — ProtoWriter now uses manual varint\n  encoding with no external proto library required\n• Verified working: Grafana Loki 3.4.1, Jaeger 1.65.0, OTel Collector 0.164.0\n\nv1.0.0 — Initial release\n• OtlpLogSink — OTLP log export via binary Protobuf over gRPC (port 4317) or HTTP (port 4318)\n• PII masking in-process before OTLP export — CorrelationId, UserId, RequestPath, ElapsedMs on every record\n• OtlpProtocol enum — Grpc and HttpProtobuf\n• AddSinkSharpTracing() — distributed tracing registration via configureTracing callback\n• OtlpSuppressingHandler — prevents instrumentation from tracing the sink's own export calls\n• Supported backends: Jaeger, Grafana Loki, Datadog, New Relic, Honeycomb, Azure Monitor\nSee full changelog: https://github.com/SinkSharp/CHANGELOG.md",
